\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Opus 4.7 does exactly what you ask it to do. Which turns out to be a problem if your workflow depended on the old model guessing what you actually meant.\
I\'92ve spent four days testing this release \'97 migration benchmarks against GPT-5.4, a real afternoon inside Claude Design, and a steady stream of production work \'97 and what I found is that the backlash and the praise are both describing real things. The model is measurably stronger on the hardest work. It\'92s also more combative, more literal, and quietly more expensive per unit of output even though the sticker price didn\'92t change. Those aren\'92t side effects of the same decision. They\'92re separate engineering choices that shipped in the same release, and they have separate fixes. The people treating this as one story are going to make the wrong call on migration. Some of you will overpay for work that got cheaper. Others will downgrade away from the one model that actually got the hard stuff right.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa400\partightenfactor0

